# Database & Migrations

## Schema Source of Truth

`lib/db/src/schema/schema.ts` is the single source of truth for all database tables. All Drizzle ORM table definitions live here. Do not define schema elsewhere.

## ORM Driver

The api-server uses `drizzle-orm/node-postgres` (standard pg pool).
- Do NOT use the Neon HTTP driver (`drizzle-orm/neon-http`) — this project uses a standard Postgres DB.
- DB connection and migration helpers are in `artifacts/api-server/src/db.ts`.

## Running Migrations

**Interactive (dev only — avoid in scripts):**
```bash
pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push
```
This is interactive — it prompts about potential table renames. Always choose **"create table"** for new tables, never rename.

**Non-interactive (preferred for automation):**
```bash
pnpm --filter @workspace/db run generate   # generates SQL migration file
psql $DATABASE_URL -f lib/db/drizzle/<migration>.sql   # applies it
```

## Required Environment Variable

`DATABASE_URL` — Postgres connection string. Must be set before starting the API server.

## Data Access Pattern

All database reads/writes go through the `ExternalAPIStorage` class in `artifacts/api-server/src/storage.ts`. Add new data access methods there rather than querying directly in route handlers.

## Security

Every query that reads user or creator data must scope results to the authenticated user's ID or verify an admin role server-side. Missing row-level authorization at the API layer is the primary injection/disclosure risk (see `threat_model.md`).
